    "probe_text": "Here is the full pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class. Every step is governed by `transaction`, so the whole thing runs in one transaction that commits only after the final step.\n\n**Gate (before any step)**\n- **Authorization:** the endpoint file declares `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`, so a caller lacking that role is rejected (403) before the pipeline runs.\n\n**In order:**\n\n1. **`ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 *validation.* Binds the request body (`@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` \u2014 the only step that reads the body) and requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` to be non-null and non-blank. Any missing/blank field \u2192 **400** `MissingFieldsException` listing every offending field name. Republishes the DTO for downstream steps.\n\n2. **`ValidatePostcode`** \u2014 *validation.* Only if a `postcode` is present: it must be exactly 4 digits, and when the city maps to a known region it must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); unknown region accepts any 4-digit code. Absent postcode is left alone. Violation \u2192 **400** `MissingFieldsException(\"postcode\")`.\n\n3. **`NormalizeTelephone`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Rewrites `telephone` into E.164: keeps a leading `+`/country code if present, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; strips spaces/dashes/brackets. Then validates 8\u201315 total digits and correct national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Bad number \u2192 **400** `MissingFieldsException(\"telephone\")`. On success **mutates `request.telephone`** to the normalized `+...` value (persisted and returned).\n\n4. **`NormalizeEmail`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Only if an email is present: must match the email regex, else **400** `MissingFieldsException(\"email\")`. On success **mutates `request.email`** to lower-case. Absent/blank email is left untouched.\n\n5. **`NormalizeAddress`** \u2014 *side-effect + validation.* Trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`). If blank after normalization \u2192 **400** `MissingFieldsException(\"address\")`. **Mutates `request.address`** to the canonical form (also used by later comparisons).\n\n6. **`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** \u2014 *validation.* Scans all owners; if an existing owner matches **both** telephone and (case-insensitive) email, \u2192 **409** `DuplicateIdentityException`. (Same-household owners with different phones are allowed.)\n\n7. **`EnsureCityCapacity`** \u2014 *validation.* Counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 **50**, \u2192 **409** `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n8. **`BuildOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`. Sets `registrationDate` to the request's date or today, and if that day is Saturday/Sunday rolls it forward to Monday. Publishes the `Owner`.\n\n9. **`EnsureDailyLimit`** \u2014 *validation.* Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's (adjusted) date; if \u2265 **100**, \u2192 **429** `DailyLimitExceededException`.\n\n10. **`AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `customerCode` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is one greater than the count of owners already in that city.\n\n11. **`AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Sets `namesakeCount` to the number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive, computed before the save so it excludes this owner).\n\n12. **`SaveOwner`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n\n13. **`LogAuditOnCreate`** \u2014 *side-effect.* Emits an `AUDIT` logger line with the owner's id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and a computed `membershipLevel` (1\u20133: base 1, +1 for having an email, +1 for zero namesakes, capped at 3). The membership level is only logged, not stored.\n\n14. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *side-effect (response).* Maps the owner to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` to true when more than **80** owners share the registration day, and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n15. **Transaction commit** \u2014 because every step carries `govern: [ transaction ]`, all persistence (the save) commits once here at the end of the pipeline.\n\nA few things worth flagging: the body is bound only in step 1; `telephone`, `email`, and `address` are mutated in place on the request DTO and thus both persisted and echoed back; and `membershipLevel` (audit-only) and `bulkSignupWarning` (response-only) are derived, not stored on the entity."
  },
